# Build context exclusions.
#
# The build context is now the repo root (compose sets `context: .`), so
# without this every build would ship .git, the local .venv and — worst
# — .env with live Meta tokens and the Anthropic key into the daemon.
# The Dockerfiles only COPY specific paths, so nothing secret lands in a
# layer today, but a future broad `COPY . .` would leak them silently.
# Excluding here means that mistake can't be made.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# runtime state, not build inputs: attachments are the OCR ground truth
# and backups can be gigabytes
data/
docs/
frontend/node_modules
whatsapp-bridge/node_modules
whatsapp-bridge/.wwebjs_auth
whatsapp-bridge/.wwebjs_cache

*.md
!README.md
